What It Is
A provenance-aware, versioned repository of non-fiction works. The STAG annotation layer and the Null-Model Protocol statistical layer are built in. Users deposit works. The repository stores the works, the annotations, the statistical results, and the provenance. It reuses the STAG schema library (App 17), the Null-Model Protocol library (App 18), the PROV-O exporter (App 3), the provenance database (App 20), and the combined workbench (App 14). It is a sibling of the STAG and Null-Model infrastructure, not a replacement. It is for researchers, labs, consortia, and anyone depositing non-fiction works.

Core Requirements
Functional requirements:

Accept deposits of non-fiction works from users.

Store the works, their metadata, their provenance, and their files.

Provide the STAG annotation layer: each work can be annotated with STAG records.

Provide the Null-Model Protocol statistical layer: each work can be linked to Null-Model Protocol results.

Validate every deposit against the deposit schema.

Validate every STAG annotation against the STAG schema (Artifact 2, Appendix B.1) and the thirty-two semantic rules.

Validate every Null-Model Protocol result against the Null-Model Protocol schema (from App 8 and App 9).

Enforce provenance completeness: every deposit has a depositor, a date, a source, and a tool version.

Enforce versioning: every deposit has a version, and updates create new versions.

Enforce supersession acyclicity.

Support querying by work ID, title, authors, date, publisher, identifiers, work type, language, license, depositor, deposit date, keywords, STAG label, STAG anchoring status, Null-Model Protocol exceedance probability, and flag.

Support full-text search of the abstract, the keywords, the notes, and the STAG evidence fields.

Support aggregation queries: count by work type, by language, by year, by depositor, by STAG label, by anchoring status.

Support exporting a work as JSON, PROV-O, and Turtle.

Support importing a work from JSON.

Support bulk import and bulk export.

Support a REST API for CRUD operations.

Support a GraphQL API for flexible queries.

Support a command-line interface for administration.

Support authentication and authorization.

Support audit logging.

Support backup and restore.

Support a web interface for depositing, browsing, and querying.

Support moderation: deposits can be marked as pending, approved, or rejected.

Support licensing: each work has a license.

Support citation: each work has a citation.

Support export to common formats: BibTeX, RIS, CSL-JSON.

Non-functional requirements:

Deterministic: same inputs produce same outputs.

Fast: query a typical work in under 100 milliseconds; aggregate over 10,000 works in under one second.

Scalable: support up to 10^6 works.

Versioned: the library records the STAG schema version, the Null-Model Protocol schema version, the deposit schema version, and the library version.

Reproducible: the library records the provenance for every deposit.

Portable: works on Linux, macOS, and Windows.

Well-documented: API documentation, deposit schema documentation, and user guide.

Input Specification
Input 1. Work deposit. Required for create and update operations. A deposit object conforming to the deposit schema.

Input 2. Files. Required for create operations. One or more files (PDF, LaTeX, plain text, structured data).

Input 3. Provenance record. Required for create and update operations. The depositor ID, the timestamp, the source, and the tool version.

Input 4. STAG annotations. Optional. One or more STAG records.

Input 5. Null-Model Protocol results. Optional. One or more Null-Model Protocol results.

Input 6. Query. Required for read operations. A query object with fields for work ID, title, authors, date, publisher, identifiers, work type, language, license, depositor, deposit date, keywords, STAG label, STAG anchoring status, Null-Model Protocol exceedance probability, and flag.

Input 7. Aggregation query. Required for aggregation operations. A query object with fields for the aggregation dimension and the filter.

Input 8. Authentication credentials. Required for authenticated operations.

Input 9. Bulk import file. Optional. A file containing multiple deposits in JSON or JSON Lines format.

Input 10. Bulk export query. Optional. A query object selecting the works to export.

Output Specification
Output 1. Work record. JSON. The work as stored, including metadata, provenance, STAG annotations, and Null-Model Protocol results.

Output 2. PROV-O serialization. Turtle or JSON-LD. The work mapped to PROV-O.

Output 3. Turtle serialization. Turtle. The work as an RDF graph.

Output 4. Citation. BibTeX, RIS, or CSL-JSON. The citation for the work.

Output 5. Query result. JSON. The list of works matching the query, with pagination.

Output 6. Aggregation result. JSON. The counts by the aggregation dimension.

Output 7. Full-text search result. JSON. The list of works matching the search query.

Output 8. Bulk export file. JSON or JSON Lines. The works matching the bulk export query.

Output 9. Audit log entry. JSON. The operation, the work ID, the depositor, the timestamp, and the result.

Output 10. API response. JSON. The result of the API operation, with HTTP status.

Output 11. GraphQL response. JSON. The result of the GraphQL query.

Output 12. Backup file. A database dump or a JSON archive.

Module-by-Module Specification
Module 1: Deposit Schema
The deposit schema defines the structure of a work deposit. It has the following fields:

work_id (string, required)

title (string, required)

authors (array of strings, required)

date (ISO8601, required)

publisher (string, optional)

identifiers (object: DOI, ISBN, arXiv ID, other)

work_type (book, paper, preprint, report, dataset, other)

language (string)

license (string)

deposit_date (ISO8601, required)

depositor_id (string, required)

depositor_affiliation (string, optional)

provenance (object: source, tool_version, notes)

stag_annotations (array of STAG records, optional)

null_model_results (array of Null-Model Protocol results, optional)

files (array of file objects: path, hash, size, format)

abstract (string, optional)

keywords (array of strings, optional)

notes (string, optional)

moderation_status (pending, approved, rejected; default pending)

version (integer; default 1)

supersedes (string, optional)

superseded_by (string, optional)

citation (string, optional)

Module 2: Database Schema
The database has the following tables:

work. Holds the work records. Fields: work_id (primary key), title, authors, date, publisher, identifiers, work_type, language, license, deposit_date, depositor_id, depositor_affiliation, provenance, abstract, keywords, notes, moderation_status, version, supersedes, superseded_by, citation, created_at, updated_at.

file. Holds the file records. Fields: file_id (primary key), work_id (foreign key to work), path, hash, size, format, created_at.

stag_annotation. Holds the STAG annotation records. Fields: annotation_id (primary key), work_id (foreign key to work), record_json, derived_display_label, evidential_anchoring_status, not_determinable_flag, provisional_flag, threshold_sensitive_flag, regime_not_determinable, identity_partition_sensitive, created_at, updated_at.

null_model_result. Holds the Null-Model Protocol results. Fields: result_id (primary key), work_id (foreign key to work), result_json, observed_statistic, exceedance_probability, monte_carlo_uncertainty, empty_w_fraction, point_mass_at_zero, tail_definition, N, created_at, updated_at.

provenance. Holds the provenance records. Fields: provenance_id (primary key), work_id (foreign key to work), depositor_id, depositor_affiliation, timestamp, source, tool_version, operation (create, update, delete), created_at.

audit_log. Holds the audit log entries. Fields: audit_id (primary key), operation, record_type, record_id, depositor_id, timestamp, result, details, created_at.

moderation. Holds the moderation records. Fields: moderation_id (primary key), work_id (foreign key to work), moderator_id, moderation_status, moderation_date, moderation_notes, created_at.

Module 3: Deposit Loader
Reads a work deposit from a JSON file or an API request. Validates it against the deposit schema. Validates any STAG annotations against the STAG schema. Validates any Null-Model Protocol results against the Null-Model Protocol schema. Rejects malformed deposits with an error.

Module 4: Deposit Writer
Writes a work deposit to the database. Inserts into the work, file, stag_annotation, null_model_result, provenance, and moderation tables. Enforces referential integrity.

Module 5: Deposit Reader
Reads a work deposit from the database. Joins the tables to reconstruct the full deposit. Returns the deposit as JSON.

Module 6: Deposit Updater
Updates a work deposit. Creates a new version. Inserts a new provenance record. Updates the work table.

Module 7: Deposit Deleter
Deletes a work deposit. Marks it as deleted (soft delete) or removes it (hard delete, based on configuration). Inserts an audit log entry.

Module 8: Query Engine
Executes queries against the database. Supports queries by work ID, title, authors, date, publisher, identifiers, work type, language, license, depositor, deposit date, keywords, STAG label, STAG anchoring status, Null-Model Protocol exceedance probability, and flag. Supports pagination.

Module 9: Full-Text Search Engine
Executes full-text search against the abstract, the keywords, the notes, and the STAG evidence fields. Uses the database's full-text search capabilities (PostgreSQL tsvector, SQLite FTS5, or a dedicated search engine).

Module 10: Aggregation Engine
Executes aggregation queries. Supports counts by work type, language, year, depositor, STAG label, and anchoring status.

Module 11: Exporter
Exports a work as JSON, PROV-O, and Turtle. Uses the PROV-O exporter (App 3) for the PROV-O and Turtle formats. Exports the citation as BibTeX, RIS, or CSL-JSON.

Module 12: Importer
Imports a work from JSON. Uses the deposit loader and the deposit writer.

Module 13: Bulk Import and Export
Imports multiple works from a JSON or JSON Lines file. Exports multiple works to a JSON or JSON Lines file.

Module 14: REST API
Provides the REST API. Endpoints:

GET /works. List works with pagination and filters.

GET /works/{id}. Get a work by ID.

POST /works. Create a work.

PUT /works/{id}. Update a work.

DELETE /works/{id}. Delete a work.

GET /works/{id}/provo. Get a work as PROV-O.

GET /works/{id}/turtle. Get a work as Turtle.

GET /works/{id}/citation. Get a work's citation in BibTeX, RIS, or CSL-JSON.

GET /works/{id}/stag. Get a work's STAG annotations.

GET /works/{id}/null-model. Get a work's Null-Model Protocol results.

POST /query. Execute a query.

POST /aggregate. Execute an aggregation query.

POST /search. Execute a full-text search.

POST /bulk/import. Bulk import works.

POST /bulk/export. Bulk export works.

POST /moderate/{id}. Moderate a work (approve or reject).

GET /audit. List audit log entries.

Module 15: GraphQL API
Provides the GraphQL API. The schema exposes the same entities as the REST API, with the ability to traverse the relationships between them (work to STAG annotations, work to Null-Model Protocol results, work to files, work to provenance).

Module 16: Command-Line Interface
Provides the command-line interface for administration:

db init. Initialize the database.

db migrate. Run migrations.

db backup. Backup the database.

db restore. Restore the database.

db import. Import works.

db export. Export works.

db query. Execute a query.

db aggregate. Execute an aggregation query.

db moderate. Moderate a work.

db audit. List audit log entries.

Module 17: Authentication and Authorization
Provides authentication (API keys, OAuth, or JWT) and authorization (role-based access control: reader, depositor, moderator, admin).

Module 18: Audit Logging
Logs every operation (create, update, delete, query, moderate) with the depositor, the timestamp, the result, and the details.

Module 19: Backup and Restore
Provides backup and restore. Backup produces a database dump or a JSON archive. Restore loads the backup.

Module 20: Web Interface
Provides a web interface for depositing, browsing, and querying. Displays works, their STAG annotations, and their Null-Model Protocol results. Provides a search box, a filter panel, an aggregation view, and a deposit form.

Module 21: Moderation Workflow
Provides a moderation workflow. Deposits are created with moderation_status = pending. A moderator can approve or reject a deposit. The moderation status is recorded in the moderation table.

Module 22: Citation Generator
Generates a citation for a work in BibTeX, RIS, or CSL-JSON. Uses the work's metadata (title, authors, date, publisher, identifiers, license).

Module 23: Migration Manager
Manages database migrations. Each deposit schema version has a migration script. Migrations are applied in order.

